{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Elohim, You</b> — true judgment." "<b>You know</b> — whether I was a fool." "<b>and my guilt</b> — to these enemies, whether unintentionally or intentionally, as my enemies will falsely mention." "<b>And for my folly</b> with a lamed — they added the lamed in הרגו לאבנר (2 Samuel 3:30)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 69, :notes {3 "The comparison is to the superfluous lamed in לאבנר; Ibn Ezra reads both cases as an added lamed not required by syntax."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:22.607666727Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}